"Update privacy" = "Update checks contact public GitHub over HTTPS. GitHub sees your IP address and ordinary HTTP metadata. Clipboard contents and system profiling are never sent. Downloads start only after you choose Update. Change this in Settings.";
"About privacy" = "Unlimited pins, only your last 3 distinct text copies. Pins are stored locally as plain text. Recent copies disappear on quit. No clipboard uploads or analytics. Marked private/password/transient contents are skipped; unmarked sensitive text cannot be identified.\n\nClick a pin to copy and close; click a recent copy to pin. Drag to the nearby trash icon to delete; release elsewhere or press Esc to cancel. Deletion can be undone.\n\nKeyboard: ↑ ↓ / Tab to select, Return to activate, ⌘Delete to delete, ⌘Z to undo, ⌘, for Settings, ⌘Q to quit, Esc to close.\n\nmacOS 13+. No auto-start or extra permissions. With permission, update checks contact public GitHub only, without clipboard data or system profiling.";
